WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:03.540
- I mean, literally, on
a seat, fire blazing,

00:00:03.540 --> 00:00:05.689
smoke going, inside the train.

00:00:05.689 --> 00:00:08.189
(eerie music)

00:00:11.320 --> 00:00:12.280
- So, I was heading to work.

00:00:12.280 --> 00:00:13.570
So, I was taking the six train.

00:00:13.570 --> 00:00:15.270
So, this was primetime rush hour.

00:00:15.270 --> 00:00:16.550
There's barely any seats.

00:00:16.550 --> 00:00:17.990
Everyone's kind of in a miserable mood.

00:00:17.990 --> 00:00:19.760
I ended up getting all the way

00:00:19.760 --> 00:00:22.500
at the edge of the train where
the window is right here.

00:00:22.500 --> 00:00:23.550
Then, there's a little space,

00:00:23.550 --> 00:00:24.880
and then, there's another cab.

00:00:24.880 --> 00:00:26.790
I'm sitting with my girlfriend,
and she's talking to me.

00:00:26.790 --> 00:00:28.190
And I kind of zone out for a second.

00:00:28.190 --> 00:00:30.520
I'm staring through the
window into the other car.

00:00:30.520 --> 00:00:32.390
And then, I see this lady
coming towards the door.

00:00:32.390 --> 00:00:33.560
I don't really think anything of it.

00:00:33.560 --> 00:00:34.920
I'm kind of just like bracing

00:00:34.920 --> 00:00:36.910
'cause I get a little nervous
when the doors open up.

00:00:36.910 --> 00:00:38.670
So, I'm bracing for the
other door to open up,

00:00:38.670 --> 00:00:39.680
and it doesn't open up.

00:00:39.680 --> 00:00:40.620
Where is this lady?

00:00:40.620 --> 00:00:42.870
So, I see her in the
middle of the train cars.

00:00:42.870 --> 00:00:44.830
So, I'm looking around, and
no one else is noticing.

00:00:44.830 --> 00:00:45.720
So, I'm getting a little nervous.

00:00:45.720 --> 00:00:46.790
I go to my girlfriend, I was like,

00:00:46.790 --> 00:00:48.700
"Did you see this person in
the middle of the train?"

00:00:48.700 --> 00:00:50.280
She's like, "Yeah, what of it?"

00:00:50.280 --> 00:00:51.200
And I was like, "All right, never mind."

00:00:51.200 --> 00:00:53.100
I go back to listening to the story.

00:00:53.100 --> 00:00:54.530
And then, I look out the window again,

00:00:54.530 --> 00:00:56.990
and this lady has now
dropped her trousers,

00:00:56.990 --> 00:00:59.950
and is using the restroom in the middle

00:00:59.950 --> 00:01:01.070
of the train right there.

00:01:01.070 --> 00:01:03.130
And not just number one, but number two.

00:01:03.130 --> 00:01:05.770
It was in between the two train cars,

00:01:05.770 --> 00:01:07.800
while moving in the danger zone.

00:01:07.800 --> 00:01:09.910
And where I'm sitting is actually

00:01:09.910 --> 00:01:11.900
a very terrible vantage point.

00:01:11.900 --> 00:01:13.530
But the worst part about the whole story

00:01:13.530 --> 00:01:15.190
is I'm looking in the other train,

00:01:15.190 --> 00:01:17.250
and I'm looking around,
looking at my girlfriend,

00:01:17.250 --> 00:01:19.220
and I was like, "Is anybody
else seeing this right now?

00:01:19.220 --> 00:01:20.310
"Or is it just me?"

00:01:20.310 --> 00:01:22.290
As soon as I figure out what's going on,

00:01:22.290 --> 00:01:23.990
I tap her on the shoulder,
I'm like, "Look."

00:01:23.990 --> 00:01:25.620
But she's already done.

00:01:25.620 --> 00:01:27.980
Pulls up her trousers, goes
back in the other train,

00:01:27.980 --> 00:01:28.970
sits back down.

00:01:28.970 --> 00:01:31.730
And I swear to you, that
the person she sat next to,

00:01:31.730 --> 00:01:33.460
gave this horrific look like

00:01:33.460 --> 00:01:35.020
he just smelled like something died.

00:01:35.020 --> 00:01:37.120
And I was just like,
well, I'm the only one

00:01:37.120 --> 00:01:38.870
that noticed that just happened.

00:01:38.870 --> 00:01:40.010
- I was East Village.

00:01:40.010 --> 00:01:41.890
I was gonna take the F
train back into Queens.

00:01:41.890 --> 00:01:43.830
It was two in the morning,
2:30 in the morning.

00:01:43.830 --> 00:01:45.650
And the train came in,
I hopped in the car.

00:01:45.650 --> 00:01:48.250
Everyone started hearing
people yelling, "Fire, fire!"

00:01:48.250 --> 00:01:50.170
Clearly, we weren't going
to be going anywhere.

00:01:50.170 --> 00:01:51.460
But I like held on hope.

00:01:51.460 --> 00:01:52.810
I was like, "I'm just gonna sit here.

00:01:52.810 --> 00:01:54.020
"This might just be a fluke."

00:01:54.020 --> 00:01:55.620
It wasn't a fluke, everyone got out.

00:01:55.620 --> 00:01:58.020
It was two cars down, there was smoke.

00:01:58.020 --> 00:02:00.000
I actually had a friend
that was on the other side

00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:00.870
that called me and was like,

00:02:00.870 --> 00:02:03.310
"Hey, there's a legit fire in the car."

00:02:03.310 --> 00:02:04.370
And I was like, "Oh."
(censor beeps)

00:02:04.370 --> 00:02:07.090
So, I ran over to the
car, and true to form,

00:02:07.090 --> 00:02:08.160
there was a crowd of people.

00:02:08.160 --> 00:02:11.150
Their phones were whipped
out, I whip out my phone.

00:02:11.150 --> 00:02:13.200
And there was a fire on
the seat of the train.

00:02:13.200 --> 00:02:15.460
None of us left, a
bunch of us just stayed.

00:02:15.460 --> 00:02:16.640
When you got out of the station,

00:02:16.640 --> 00:02:18.180
there were firetrucks everywhere.

00:02:18.180 --> 00:02:20.680
And they had closed down a couple streets.

00:02:20.680 --> 00:02:22.570
And clearly, I wasn't gonna get home.

00:02:22.570 --> 00:02:25.120
It was just random, and entertaining,

00:02:25.120 --> 00:02:26.190
even though I probably shouldn't

00:02:26.190 --> 00:02:27.480
have thought of it that way.

00:02:27.480 --> 00:02:29.150
- I recently moved to New York.

00:02:29.150 --> 00:02:30.870
So, I'm not super familiar with the city.

00:02:30.870 --> 00:02:32.770
And I'm just kind of going about my way.

00:02:32.770 --> 00:02:34.640
And my commute to work, at this time,

00:02:34.640 --> 00:02:37.040
was probably about 30 to 40 minutes.

00:02:37.040 --> 00:02:39.550
And as I was walking on

00:02:40.400 --> 00:02:44.320
the platform, I was approaching
some quite steep stairs.

00:02:44.320 --> 00:02:47.450
And suddenly, this like enormous pressure

00:02:47.450 --> 00:02:49.430
smacked me in the back of the neck.

00:02:49.430 --> 00:02:52.830
And I fell to the
ground, I just collapsed.

00:02:52.830 --> 00:02:54.610
I didn't actually really have the time

00:02:54.610 --> 00:02:56.740
to like turn around and
figure out what had gone on

00:02:56.740 --> 00:02:58.170
because my phone was smashed,

00:02:58.170 --> 00:02:59.490
my bag had fallen down on the floor,

00:02:59.490 --> 00:03:00.460
and everyone was looking.

00:03:00.460 --> 00:03:02.300
What had happened is this guy,

00:03:02.300 --> 00:03:05.420
he had said that I had barged into him,

00:03:05.420 --> 00:03:06.710
previously on my commute.

00:03:06.710 --> 00:03:09.560
And he had turned around,
got himself very worked up,

00:03:09.560 --> 00:03:13.020
and found me, and ran, at full speed,

00:03:13.020 --> 00:03:16.010
pushed me super, super hard
in the back of my neck.

00:03:16.010 --> 00:03:17.100
So, I fell down.

00:03:17.100 --> 00:03:18.720
So, at this point, I've turned around,

00:03:18.720 --> 00:03:20.060
not really knowing what's going on.

00:03:20.060 --> 00:03:22.440
I looked up at him, and he was seething,

00:03:22.440 --> 00:03:25.870
incredibly angry, kind of glazed over,

00:03:25.870 --> 00:03:28.970
kind of like some alpha male
character in a mud film.

00:03:28.970 --> 00:03:31.210
But he was still angry and still proud.

00:03:31.210 --> 00:03:33.530
So, he was like standing
over me going (pants).

00:03:35.091 --> 00:03:38.160
(laughs) And I was like, "Hey, hon."

00:03:38.160 --> 00:03:40.840
He was like, "You just barged into me!"

00:03:40.840 --> 00:03:43.130
So, I was like, apologizing profusely.

00:03:43.130 --> 00:03:46.050
This guy just kept repeating
that I had barged into him.

00:03:46.050 --> 00:03:48.490
Someone else asked him to calm down.

00:03:48.490 --> 00:03:50.620
Someone else was helping
me up off the floor.

00:03:50.620 --> 00:03:52.030
And then, I apologized.

00:03:52.030 --> 00:03:54.040
I said, "Listen, I'm really sorry."

00:03:54.040 --> 00:03:55.550
And then, he went to work.

00:03:55.550 --> 00:03:58.900
And then, I went to work,
and just sat at my desk,

00:03:58.900 --> 00:04:00.680
had a cup of tea, and didn't tell anyone.

00:04:00.680 --> 00:04:02.720
And then, a couple days
later, I was like (chuckles),

00:04:02.720 --> 00:04:04.960
"Actually, that was really dramatic."

00:04:04.960 --> 00:04:07.460
(eerie music)

